<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρα-πτερυλλίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>four-wing</i>, i.e.
				<i>grasshopper</i> or <i>locust</i>, 
				Boeot.
			 word in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				871
			</span></i>: Elmsl. thinks that by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν
				ὀρταλίχων ἢ τῶν τετραπτερυλλίδων</span> is intended
			birds and <i>beasts</i>; no doubt this is so, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραπτερυλλίδων</span> being brought in
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ ὑπόνοιαν</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραπόδων</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
